# ADR-000: Bootstrap

## Status

Accepted on bootstrap.

## Context

`{{ project_name }}` was created from the `library-dotnet` Copier template at `ika100/sdlc-foundry`. The template encodes the platform's .NET library conventions (platform ADR-125, ADR-127, spec 221):

- .NET {{ dotnet_major }} LTS SDK via devbox; C# with nullable reference types, central package versions and lock files
- One packable project `src/{{ namespace }}` (NuGet package `{{ namespace }}`, target framework `net{{ dotnet_major }}.0`) and its test project
- `dotnet format` + the .NET analyzers (warnings are errors) as the quality gate; trivy for the locked packages
- xUnit with an 80 % line coverage gate (coverlet)
- The release tag is the version: the tag's `publish` CI job packs the library and pushes it to GitHub Packages (`https://nuget.pkg.github.com/{{ github_org | lower }}/index.json`)
- No container image and no deployment
- Claude Code agents from the `sdlc-foundry` marketplace (`svc-dotnet` + `svc` + `shared`)

## Decision

We adopt the platform conventions verbatim. Any deviation must be justified in a new ADR.

## Consequences

Skeleton updates (CI, devbox recipes, .NET bump, build and analyzer settings) arrive through `copier update`; `src/`, `tests/`, `Directory.Packages.props`, the solution and `docs/adr/` are project-owned and never overwritten.
